SRC/taxlaw -- taxlaw, as built for OS-9/68000=============================================taxlaw writes sentences of imitation tax regulation, with section andparagraph references: `taxlaw 3' writes three.  The author is notnamed; the shell archive is dated 31 July 1990.  From the `silly'collection posted to alt.sources in December 1992.ORIG holds taxmain.c, taxlaw.c, index.c, wrap.c, rnd.c and the makefileas posted.Every source is unchanged.  The program defines its own index(), asubstring search, and the linker takes it before the library's.  rand()is linked from /dd/LIB/rand.r.    taxlaw 1